# Fix dogan.xaigrok.ir 503 (dogan-webui down)

- **Timestamp:** 2026-07-24 21:15 +03:30
- **Host:** t3-new (`ssh t3` → cloud-admin@2.144.27.74)
- **URL:** https://dogan.xaigrok.ir/

## Cause

HAProxy routes `dogan.xaigrok.ir` → `dogan-webui:80`. Container was `Exited (255)` because:

`failed to set up container networking: could not find a network matching network mode parkiroid-net: network parkiroid-net not found`

API stack (`dogan-api`, `dogan-pgsql`, `livekit`) was healthy on `t3-net`; only the web UI was down.

## Commands

1. Inspected `dogan-webui` state, logs, and networks
2. Temporarily created `parkiroid-net` and started the old container; verified HAProxy → webui
3. Recreated container permanently on `t3-net`:
   - `docker stop` / rename old → `dogan-webui-broken-parkiroid-net`
   - `docker run -d --name dogan-webui --restart unless-stopped --network t3-net -v /cloud-admin/docker-volumes/parkiroid-web:/data:rw parkiroid-web:latest`
   - Removed old container and unused `parkiroid-net`
4. Verified `https://dogan.xaigrok.ir/` → HTTP 200

## Result

`dogan-webui` is Up on `t3-net`; public site returns 200.

## Warnings

- Web UI image is still `parkiroid-web:latest` (legacy name); not part of the `dogan` Compose deploy in this repo
- Prefer keeping webui on `t3-net` only so HAProxy DNS resolution keeps working after reboots
